        {
          "id": 2936451394,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I don't understand.  It's currently documented in https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsdg_html/#lua_class_DissectorTable, section 13.3.2.11, which indicates that it returns, _\"Number of bytes dissected. Note that some dissectors always return number of bytes in incoming buffer, so be aware.\"_  If the intended dissector doesn't dissect it, then it's wrong to automatically pass it to the generic data dissector; otherwise we'll never get a return value of 0, meaning that no bytes were dissected, and then we can never attempt to try another dissector.  Isn't this the whole point of the **`try`** in `dissectortable:try()`?\n\nWhat would you suggest the documentation be updated to say then?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6624779,
            "username": "cjmaynard",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Christopher Maynard",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6624779/avatar.png?v=1788529529",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/cjmaynard"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-12-05T18:47:29.809Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-12-10T10:08:00.053Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 438473751,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2025-12-10T10:08:00.053Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 22633,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2937808746,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I did a lot of git blaming to find that the first version of DissectorTable_try is an homage to Star Wars' Yoda (\"Do or do not. There is no try.\")\nWhat I'm unsure of is when the data dissector will be called if bytes are left undissected.  And do we have to document that every Lua script that now calls DissectorTable_try also has to explicitly call the data dissector?  That's what I meant about updating the documentation (maybe it's just release notes and not the function itself?)",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-12-07T15:15:17.850Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-12-10T10:08:00.053Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 438473751,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
