          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 22633,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2940011290,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The current behavior deviates from the C equivalent `dissector_try_uint()`, where that function does **not** call the data dissector.  You are expected to check the return value and take whatever other action you want based on its value.  It's my strong opinion that the Lua implementation is wrong and should be corrected by this merge request, which would also make it behave more similarly to C.\n\nTo help drive home the point, take the example from [`packet-zmtp.c:dissect_zmtp_data()`](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/dissectors/packet-zmtp.c#L308) where it first tries with the destination port, then with the source port and then calls the data dissector.  This wouldn't be possible to do with the current Lua implementation.\n\nAll that said, I suppose an optional Boolean argument could be added to `dissectortable:try()` to tell it to call the data dissector if everything else fails?  But the default should be **not** to automatically call it - the same as `dissector_try_uint()`.\n\n**EDIT**: I think it's fine to update the release notes to document the change in behavior.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6624779,
            "username": "cjmaynard",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Christopher Maynard",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6624779/avatar.png?v=1788529529",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/cjmaynard"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-12-08T16:52:45.327Z",
